&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49171782</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 17:09:45 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Ask HN: Can we direct AI on our personal projects during work hours?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49171630</link><description>&lt;p&gt;So here's the question I wanted to pose around AI usage. With modern advanced AI, much of the time, using AI consists of sending a message a waiting a long time (often an hour or more) before the AI finishes a task.&lt;p&gt;Which I think brings up an important question, is it okay to take short work breaks to send instructions to AI working on your personal projects during work hours?&lt;p&gt;Do any employers have policies around this? And how does it interact with legal standards?&lt;p&gt;Are the rules around work-product well suited to the modern AI age?&lt;p&gt;Does it matter if I'm hourly vs salaried?&lt;p&gt;Should we do the same thing for work (asking work AI to do things occasionally during personal time)?&lt;/p&gt;
